<script type="text/javascript">
    // The walk builds the octahedron in the order the proof does: the
    // semicircle on AB bisected at C with CD and DB, the square EFGH on DB
    // with its diagonals, KL and KM through K at right angles to the square,
    // the eight joins to L and M; then the semicircle on LM through E,
    // carried round to sweep out the sphere through F, G and H.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the square only as the bases of the two pyramids
    // Lpyr and Mpyr, the joins only as their edges, and KL, KM only as the
    // one line LM, so the square outline EFGHs, the joins LE … MH, and KL,
    // KM are solid slide twins, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden); the
    // pyramids join the walk once the octahedron is constructed and LM once
    // the semicircle is described on it. A polyhedron and a sphere draw no
    // highlight, so the octahedron is lit as two faceless octagons that
    // between them walk its twelve edges (oct1, oct2), and the sphere as a
    // faceless circle on its outline (sphT); semiT is a faceless twin of the
    // filled semicircle ADB (#140). A sector draws only in the screen plane,
    // so the semicircle on LM is lit as the great circle it lies on, in the
    // plane through E (LEMc). Everything else added is transparent.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B (lineSliders, givens),
    // K (free; the centre), E (sphereSlider), F (circleSlider). K, E and F
    // arrive mid-walk and are deferred. C, D, G, H, L, M are derived and
    // listed per slide.
